    A play's static picture gives the scene's mobjects their state at its capture
    
    The static list is flattened to the leaves with points, so a surface's
    faces arrive without their surface, which the frame description now finds
    among the scene's roots: it reads the surface's faces, grid and state.
    Drawing the static picture gave only the static list its recorded state,
    so those reads took the surface as the scene holds it when the picture is
    drawn. A picture drawn once the scene has run (plays that waited for the
    render's workers) grouped the faces the scene left, not the ones the play
    held, and the draw-reads tracer reported every such read.
    
    The static picture now shows the capture's draw list as well as its static
    list, as a frame painted from the record already does.
    
    (cherry picked from commit f1b41d6d0bf05f5f1237e686b74fc7bbb3e43fba)

